your rendezvous up one night?

773
00:38:46,658 --> 00:38:47,635
Correct.

774
00:38:47,659 --> 00:38:48,659
Hmm.

775
00:38:49,661 --> 00:38:52,873
Did, uh... Did you
both get massages?

776
00:38:52,897 --> 00:38:55,009
Yes, we did.

777
00:38:55,033 --> 00:38:56,177
Uh-huh.

778
00:38:56,201 --> 00:38:57,344
So, let's see.

779
00:38:57,368 --> 00:39:03,517
The masseuse was
in the suite from 6:30...

780
00:39:03,541 --> 00:39:05,219
to 8:30.

781
00:39:05,243 --> 00:39:06,587
That right?

782
00:39:06,611 --> 00:39:07,788
- That's correct.
- Yeah.

783
00:39:07,812 --> 00:39:09,056
Each massage takes an hour?

784
00:39:09,080 --> 00:39:10,691
Yes.

785
00:39:10,715 --> 00:39:11,759
Who went first?

786
00:39:11,783 --> 00:39:14,461
- Amanda.
- Amanda.

787
00:39:14,485 --> 00:39:18,766
So while the masseuse was
giving Amanda her massage,

788
00:39:18,790 --> 00:39:21,936
you waited in-in the other
room, and then vice versa.

789
00:39:21,960 --> 00:39:23,437
- Is that right?
- Correct.

790
00:39:23,461 --> 00:39:24,872
You know what that means?

791
00:39:24,896 --> 00:39:29,043
That means that while Amanda
was getting her massage,

792
00:39:29,067 --> 00:39:31,178
between 6:30 and 7:30,

793
00:39:31,202 --> 00:39:33,113
you could have left the hotel,

794
00:39:33,137 --> 00:39:35,950
driven to Mr. Dobbs'
office, shot him,

795
00:39:35,974 --> 00:39:37,518
driven back in plenty of
time for your massage,

796
00:39:37,542 --> 00:39:39,153
and no one would
have been the wiser.

797
00:39:39,177 --> 00:39:40,088
Isn't that right?

798
00:39:40,112 --> 00:39:41,355
I did no such thing.

799
00:39:41,379 --> 00:39:43,390
I'm afraid that's
exactly what you did.

800
00:39:43,414 --> 00:39:45,626
You set the whole thing up.

801
00:39:45,650 --> 00:39:49,096
You called my client, left
a message at his motel,

802
00:39:49,120 --> 00:39:51,565
supposedly from Eugene Dobbs,

803
00:39:51,589 --> 00:39:53,300
telling him to meet

804
00:39:53,324 --> 00:39:55,903
at a sushi bar
instead of his office.

805
00:39:55,927 --> 00:39:57,371
- I did not.
- And then

806
00:39:57,395 --> 00:39:59,373
you selected a
cane from the room

807
00:39:59,397 --> 00:40:00,975
at your... at your park

808
00:40:00,999 --> 00:40:02,810
where you keep
your medical supplies,

809
00:40:02,834 --> 00:40:07,681
and put on a-a Baxter University
red Bulldog cap and jacket

810
00:40:07,705 --> 00:40:09,116
so if anybody saw you,

811
00:40:09,140 --> 00:40:10,851
they'd think you
were John Kramer,

812
00:40:10,875 --> 00:40:14,788
and knowing full well that
the masseuse and Amanda

813
00:40:14,812 --> 00:40:16,490
would give you any
alibi you needed.

814
00:40:16,514 --> 00:40:17,658
- Isn't that right?
- Oh.

815
00:40:17,682 --> 00:40:19,560
Come on, look, I
signed an agreement

816
00:40:19,584 --> 00:40:22,329
to end the lawsuits.

817
00:40:22,353 --> 00:40:25,132
I had no reason to kill him.

818
00:40:25,156 --> 00:40:26,133
None.

819
00:40:26,157 --> 00:40:28,535
Your Honor, I-I object
to this line of questioning.

820
00:40:28,559 --> 00:40:29,703
Where's the proof?

821
00:40:29,727 --> 00:40:31,705
Right here. Right
here. Right here.

822
00:40:31,729 --> 00:40:33,274
Right here.

823
00:40:33,298 --> 00:40:37,711
I'd like to submit as
Defense Exhibit "A,"

824
00:40:37,735 --> 00:40:39,947
uh, this agreement

825
00:40:39,971 --> 00:40:43,384
that, uh, the-the... the
witness was just referring to

826
00:40:43,408 --> 00:40:46,787
that was taken from
Mr. Dobbs' office last night,

827
00:40:46,811 --> 00:40:49,423
and this pen set,

828
00:40:49,447 --> 00:40:52,192
which was also taken
from his office last night,

829
00:40:52,216 --> 00:40:55,529
as Defense Exhibit "B."

830
00:40:55,553 --> 00:40:57,164
Go ahead?

831
00:40:57,188 --> 00:40:58,299
Go ahead.

832
00:40:58,323 --> 00:41:04,171
Now... this-this waiver,

833
00:41:04,195 --> 00:41:08,175
in essence, is a... is a...
an agreement in writing

834
00:41:08,199 --> 00:41:11,245
that you and Mr. Dobbs agreed

835
00:41:11,269 --> 00:41:14,682
to-to stop all lawsuits
against each other,

836
00:41:14,706 --> 00:41:18,118
and it was signed by you
on the 14th of last month,

837
00:41:18,142 --> 00:41:19,586
one week before he was killed.

838
00:41:19,610 --> 00:41:20,821
That's what I've
been telling you.

839
00:41:20,845 --> 00:41:23,257
He didn't sign it. Why?

840
00:41:23,281 --> 00:41:24,425
Well, he agreed to.

841
00:41:24,449 --> 00:41:26,226
That's why I sent it to him.

842
00:41:26,250 --> 00:41:29,430
Eugene Dobbs didn't sign
it and never intended to.

843
00:41:29,454 --> 00:41:31,532
You are wrong!

844
00:41:31,556 --> 00:41:33,400
Dobbs and I had an agreement

845
00:41:33,424 --> 00:41:36,770
to put an end to the
bad blood between us.

846
00:41:36,794 --> 00:41:38,739
Now, my lawyer
drew up that form,

847
00:41:38,763 --> 00:41:40,140
I signed it.

848
00:41:40,164 --> 00:41:42,409
Then we sent it to
him for his signature.

849
00:41:42,433 --> 00:41:45,346
I agree that you wanted a truce.

850
00:41:45,370 --> 00:41:48,932
I agree that your lawyer
made up this waiver.

851
00:41:51,376 --> 00:41:55,789
But you never signed
it before it was mailed.

852
00:41:55,813 --> 00:41:59,648
Now, here's what
I'd like you to do.

853
00:42:01,285 --> 00:42:04,098
I'd like you to write your name

854
00:42:04,122 --> 00:42:06,700
on this blank piece of paper,

855
00:42:06,724 --> 00:42:10,170
just like you did
on this waiver,

856
00:42:10,194 --> 00:42:13,187
first with this ballpoint pen.

857
00:42:14,298 --> 00:42:16,665
Go ahead. Go ahead.

858
00:42:24,108 --> 00:42:25,686
Okay. Now,

859
00:42:25,710 --> 00:42:29,123
with this fountain pen that
I bought in the drugstore.

860
00:42:29,147 --> 00:42:31,139
Okay.

861
00:42:37,055 --> 00:42:38,399
Okay. Fine.

862
00:42:38,423 --> 00:42:44,838
Now... Now with the
pen the police took

863
00:42:44,862 --> 00:42:47,307
from Mr. Dobbs' office.

864
00:42:47,331 --> 00:42:48,609
Go ahead.

865
00:42:48,633 --> 00:42:50,044
Mm-hmm.

866
00:43:01,412 --> 00:43:06,683
Oh... what a
difference a pen makes.

867
00:43:08,686 --> 00:43:10,697
You see...

868
00:43:10,721 --> 00:43:14,501
the ballpoint leaves
a little, thin line.

869
00:43:14,525 --> 00:43:15,969
See there?

870
00:43:15,993 --> 00:43:21,809
And the fountain pen leaves
a kind of a thick, wide mark.

871
00:43:21,833 --> 00:43:24,745
But the pen the police
took from Mr. Dobbs' office...

872
00:43:24,769 --> 00:43:26,847
Look at that. Phew!

873
00:43:26,871 --> 00:43:31,085
Looks almost like an
artist drew your signature.

874
00:43:31,109 --> 00:43:35,522
That's because it has
such a... a good tip,

875
00:43:35,546 --> 00:43:38,525
almost like those that
the calligraphers use.

876
00:43:38,549 --> 00:43:40,727
It's real distinctive-looking.

877
00:43:40,751 --> 00:43:42,763
It's so distinctive

878
00:43:42,787 --> 00:43:44,665
that it wouldn't take an expert

879
00:43:44,689 --> 00:43:49,036
to recognize that that pen

880
00:43:49,060 --> 00:43:51,405
is what you signed
that waiver with.

881
00:43:52,864 --> 00:43:54,341
And what's more,

882
00:43:54,365 --> 00:43:57,644
Mr. Dobbs' partner,
Mr. Wheeler, and his secretary

883
00:43:57,668 --> 00:44:01,048
are ready to testify
that he received this pen

884
00:44:01,072 --> 00:44:05,119
as a gift that day, just hours
before he was murdered.

885
00:44:05,143 --> 00:44:08,255
You knew in your heart

886
00:44:08,279 --> 00:44:10,657
that he would never
sign this waiver,

887
00:44:10,681 --> 00:44:14,895
so you killed him...
to stop the lawsuits

888
00:44:14,919 --> 00:44:18,432
and to get on with
your life with his wife.

889
00:44:18,456 --> 00:44:21,535
You saw this unsigned waiver

890
00:44:21,559 --> 00:44:24,271
on his desk after you
shot him, didn't you?

891
00:44:24,295 --> 00:44:27,274
So you signed
it, dated it, filed it,

892
00:44:27,298 --> 00:44:29,309
knowing the police would find it

893
00:44:29,333 --> 00:44:31,678
and think you had
no reason to kill him.

894
00:44:31,702 --> 00:44:36,283
Then you planted the
gun in John Kramer's room,

895
00:44:36,307 --> 00:44:38,418
knowing the police would find it

896
00:44:38,442 --> 00:44:40,921
and think he <i>had</i> done it.

897
00:44:40,945 --> 00:44:42,890
What you didn't know was,

898
00:44:42,914 --> 00:44:45,993
the only two people who
had access to this pen

899
00:44:46,017 --> 00:44:48,095
that you signed the waiver with

900
00:44:48,119 --> 00:44:51,431
was Mr. Dobbs

901
00:44:51,455 --> 00:44:53,788
and the person who killed him.

902
00:44:55,593 --> 00:44:57,323
That's all. Thank
you, Your Honor.

903
00:45:07,238 --> 00:45:09,016
Hey, Les? Les...

904
00:45:09,040 --> 00:45:10,684
Hey, Les, come... Come on in.

905
00:45:10,708 --> 00:45:12,019
Come on. What...

906
00:45:12,043 --> 00:45:13,854
Where you... Where
you... Where you going?

907
00:45:13,878 --> 00:45:16,023
Where you... Where you
been? I haven't seen you.

908
00:45:16,047 --> 00:45:17,624
I was going for a walk.

909
00:45:17,648 --> 00:45:19,326
Any other questions?

910
00:45:19,350 --> 00:45:21,428
Well, are-are... are
you... are you all right?

911
00:45:21,452 --> 00:45:23,397
I see you're not
wearing the neck brace.

912
00:45:23,421 --> 00:45:24,932
What happened with that case?

913
00:45:24,956 --> 00:45:26,600
Nothing! Nothing happened!

914
00:45:26,624 --> 00:45:29,236
You didn't collect
anything? I mean, I thought...

915
00:45:29,260 --> 00:45:30,571
Well, you thought wrong!

916
00:45:30,595 --> 00:45:32,339
I didn't collect. He collected.

917
00:45:32,363 --> 00:45:33,740
The guy who sideswiped you?

918
00:45:33,764 --> 00:45:35,008
That's right.

919
00:45:35,032 --> 00:45:38,045
He claimed I pulled into
traffic without signaling.

920
00:45:38,069 --> 00:45:40,080
Huh? How do you
like that for justice

921
00:45:40,104 --> 00:45:41,548
in this land of the free?

922
00:45:41,572 --> 00:45:43,350
Well, now, Les, uh...

923
00:45:43,374 --> 00:45:47,154
The guy who did the
sideswiping gets the payoff,

924
00:45:47,178 --> 00:45:50,691
and the guy who gets
sideswiped gets it in the rear.

925
00:45:50,715 --> 00:45:51,858
Well, now...

926
00:45:51,882 --> 00:45:55,429
Little guy hasn't got a chance,
so he shouldn't even try.

927
00:45:55,453 --> 00:45:57,097
You can't fight City Hall,

928
00:45:57,121 --> 00:45:59,833
not if you're a little guy,
because you can't win.

929
00:45:59,857 --> 00:46:01,935
The cards are
stacked against you,

930
00:46:01,959 --> 00:46:04,571
and you are dead in the water.

931
00:46:04,595 --> 00:46:07,140
You're a loser, because
you're a little guy.

932
00:46:07,164 --> 00:46:08,508
You might as well quit.

933
00:46:08,532 --> 00:46:10,811
You can't win.

934
00:46:10,835 --> 00:46:11,945
Step on the little guy!

935
00:46:11,969 --> 00:46:14,014
That's the name of the game.

936
00:46:14,038 --> 00:46:15,415
Beat up on the little guy!

937
00:46:15,439 --> 00:46:17,679
Even when you're
right, you're wrong!

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
